 cooperation. The difficulty communicating ideas may be mitigated? Not sure.\n\nCandidate B: conscientious, stress handling, but uncooperative and grumpy. That seems a bigger issue.\n\nCandidate D: strong problem solving, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership, hot temper. That seems also problematic.\n\nCandidate C: strong technical and leadership, but show-off, not open to new ideas, unorganized, not good at taking criticism. That could affect adaptability and crew cooperation.\n\nWhich candidate overall best? Possibly Candidate A because reliability and positive atmosphere may outweigh communication difficulty? But communication difficulty is important for safety. However, we have no evidence of actual communication failures, just difficulty. Candidate C's leadership may offset show-off? But not open to new ideas is a serious adaptability issue for long-distance flights.\n\nI think I might argue that Candidate A's 100% reliability and positive crew atmosphere make them a strong choice, and the communication difficulty is less severe than C's show-off and lack of openness. So I could propose Candidate A.\n\nBut we need to reference facts: A is 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, quick correct decisions, calm in crisis. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nWe can argue that reliability and decision quality are paramount, and positive atmosphere indicates good crew cooperation, while communication difficulty can be addressed with training.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate A.\n\nMake sure to reference Agent 2's recommendation and explain why I differ.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate A."}
